        "original_id": "6b4da410-3443-572e-a142-b53ff40208b3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alice Munro, Lillian Hellman\n- Works: The Moons of Jupiter, The Little Foxes\n- Organizations: Macmillan of Canada, Broadway, Nobel Prize\n- Topics: short story writing, drama, screenwriting, political activism\n\nFacts:\n- Lillian Hellman was born on June 20, 1905, and she became an American dramatist and screenwriter known for Broadway success, left-wing sympathies, and political activism.\n- Alice Munro was born on July 10, 1931, née Laidlaw, and became a Canadian short story writer and Nobel Prize winner.\n- Lillian Hellman wrote The Little Foxes, a 1939 play considered a classic of 20th-century drama.\n- Alice Munro wrote The Moons of Jupiter, a book of short stories published by Macmillan of Canada in 1982.\n- Lillian Hellman died on June 30, 1984.",
